From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hamoa: fixed GIC LPI tables

Reserve 1 MiB of RAM at 0x8a0000000 and give it to the GIC as its
memory-region, so that every boot puts the LPI property and pending
tables at the same physical addresses.

A hibernation image is restored by a freshly booted kernel, which enables
LPIs with tables of its own. On the X1 GICR_CTLR.EnableLPIs can't be
cleared again, so the restored kernel can never point the redistributors
at its tables, and MSIs set up after the resume could go missing. With
the tables at a fixed address, the loader and the restored kernel agree.

The node is in hamoa.dtsi, which purwa.dtsi includes, so every Hamoa and
Purwa laptop gets it, and it replaces the Yoga Slim 7x's own copy. The
region is 512 MiB into the second DDR bank, which starts at 0x880000000
and spans 0x880000000-0xfffffffff on the 32 GB Yoga. No Hamoa or Purwa
tree reserves anything in that bank.

The kernel uses the region from linux-omarchy-aarch64 7.3-78 ("irqchip/
gic-v3-its: take the LPI tables from a reserved-memory region"). Without
that patch it is only 1 MiB reserved. Where the region is not mapped RAM,
the kernel warns and allocates the tables as before.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
index 2e1d901..acf8ddc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa.dtsi
@@ -666,6 +666,16 @@
 			hwlocks = <&tcsr_mutex 3>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * The GIC's LPI tables, at the same address in every boot, so
+		 * that a kernel restored from hibernation and the kernel that
+		 * loaded its image agree on them: the redistributors can't be
+		 * pointed at other tables once LPIs are on.
+		 */
+		gic_lpi_mem: gic-lpi-tables@8a0000000 {
+			reg = <0x8 0xa0000000 0x0 0x100000>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	qup_opp_table_100mhz: opp-table-qup100mhz {
@@ -8865,6 +8875,8 @@
 			#redistributor-regions = <1>;
 			redistributor-stride = <0x0 0x40000>;
 
+			memory-region = <&gic_lpi_mem>;
+
 			#address-cells = <2>;
 			#size-cells = <2>;
 			ranges;
-- 
